                <pb facs="1191" n="1033" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1033"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-03-24"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 24,
                    1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Wilson reports, in reply to the Department’s telegram of March 8, that the
                    Japanese Government is unwilling to have consul-general <pb facs="1192" n="1034"
                        xml:id="pg1034"/> at Seoul styled in addition agent, on the ground that
                    under the agreement between Japan and Korea all diplomatic business concerning
                    Korea is to be transacted at Tokyo, and the resident-general will treat in
                    regard to such foreign matters only as come within the scope of consular
                    functions.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
